### Secret scanning (quick task 260816-hn1) ###
# gitleaks report output. A gitleaks report contains matched secret *values* in plaintext
# even with --redact applied to the console/log stream in some report formats -- the JSON
# report's `Secret`/`Match` fields are only redacted when --redact is passed, and this path
# must never be committed regardless, since it is scratch measurement output, not a
# reviewable artifact. See 260816-hn1-MEASUREMENTS.md for why this exists and what
# redaction guarantee was actually verified empirically before any report was trusted.
.gitleaks-reports/


